---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import experiments from '../../data/experiments.json';
import results from '../../data/results.json';
import challenges from '../../data/primitive-challenges.json';
const base=import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const counts={proposed:experiments.filter(x=>x.status==='PROPOSED').length,running:experiments.filter(x=>x.status==='RUNNING').length,completed:experiments.filter(x=>x.status==='COMPLETED').length,failed:results.filter(x=>x.evidence_label==='FAILED').length,inconclusive:results.filter(x=>x.evidence_label==='INCONCLUSIVE').length,replication:results.filter(x=>x.evidence_label==='REQUIRES REPLICATION').length,challenges:challenges.length};
---
<BaseLayout title="The Moving Invariant — What survives when expression changes?">
<section class="hero"><div class="eyebrow">Public research laboratory · foundation build</div><h1>The Moving<br/>Invariant</h1><p class="lede"><strong>What survives when expression changes?</strong> The Constraint Grammar proposes 54 structural forms of completed intelligibility. This project tests whether those forms remain invariant when wording, language, context, historical linguistic systems and machine representations change.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href={`${base}experiments`}>Explore the experiments</a><a class="button secondary" href={`${base}manifesto`}>Read the founding essay</a><a class="button secondary" href={`${base}primitives`}>See what would falsify it</a></div></section>
<section><h2>The transition</h2><div class="grid"><article class="card"><div class="kicker">Previous question</div><h3>What are the forms of completed intelligibility?</h3><p>Persistence supplies the mature 6 × 3 × 3 grammar and its coordinate-generated completion structures.</p></article><article class="card"><div class="kicker">New question</div><h3>Which forms survive transformation of expression?</h3><p>The object shifts from the map itself to persistence or change as realization moves.</p></article></div></section>
<section><h2>Three founding windows</h2><div class="grid"><a class="card" href={`${base}stacking`}><div class="kicker">STACK</div><h3>Change the utterance.</h3><p>Lexical, situational and domain variation while holding a candidate coordinate.</p></a><a class="card" href={`${base}translation`}><div class="kicker">TRANSLATE</div><h3>Change the language.</h3><p>Blind cross-linguistic coordinate preservation under independently frozen resolution.</p></a><a class="card" href={`${base}creolization`}><div class="kicker">CREOLIZE</div><h3>Change what the system must carry.</h3><p>A historical hypothesis about communicative burden and recoverable distinctions.</p></a></div><p class="quote">What survives?</p></section>
<section><h2>Universality without evasion</h2><div class="callout"><h3>A 55th is a research result, not a ritual assumption.</h3><p>Finite grammar can generate indefinite expression. The claim here is structural: every completed intelligible unit at the chosen grain is hypothesized to answer the exhaustive questions supplied by the three dimensions. A challenge succeeds by producing a missing primitive, an axis failure, or an irreducible completed-unit remainder—not merely by imagining more semantic detail.</p></div></section>
<section><h2>Live research state</h2><div class="status-grid"><div class="stat"><strong>{counts.proposed}</strong><span>proposed</span></div><div class="stat"><strong>{counts.running}</strong><span>running</span></div><div class="stat"><strong>{counts.completed}</strong><span>completed</span></div><div class="stat"><strong>{counts.failed}</strong><span>failed</span></div><div class="stat"><strong>{counts.inconclusive}</strong><span>inconclusive</span></div><div class="stat"><strong>{counts.replication}</strong><span>replication needed</span></div><div class="stat"><strong>{counts.challenges}</strong><span>primitive challenges</span></div></div><p class="meta">Counts are generated only from machine-readable records present in this repository. No success count is seeded.</p></section>
</BaseLayout>
